{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1480793-demon-the-fallen-which-house-lore-were-the-most-widely-shared","id":1480793,"title":"Demon: the Fallen - Which House Lore were the most widely shared?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-05-11T19:44:41-07:00","id":1480793,"title":"Demon: the Fallen - Which House Lore were the most widely shared?","content":"In the D:tF Player\u2019s Guide it mentions how you can potentially relearn any Lore you might have known before being cast down. Which Lore were likely the most widely shared, and which ones were kept the most occluded from the other Houses. I am thinking Lore of Awakening had plenty of teachers for anyone who wanted it, while Lore of Realms was kept secret from non Slayers, save for those who directly helped with the Underworld\u2019s construction. Lore of Celestials was probably something EVERYONE was required to know at some point, at least up to Pillar of Faith. This was just a basic survival tactic when Heaven outnumbered them 2-1 and they fought against eachp other besides. Any thoughts? Which Lore would you allow a character to justify manifesting as a recollection of his past life before he went to Hell?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-11T22:17:01-07:00","id":1480801,"title":"","content":"Having the Fallen keep their secrets to themselves during the War sets them up to have to strike deals with each other in the modern day in order to learn out-of-house Lores, so I think that's definitely preferable for the roleplaying opportunities it creates. It's easy to imagine Faction loyalty or even geographical conveniece mattering more than House of origin when the modern Demon decides who their friends are, so sharing might be something they feel a little more free to do now as well as a good way of forming bonds and alliances.<br /> <br /> That said, the Malefactors stand out. The Lore of the Forge has this weird synergy with other Lores, in that the more Lores the Malefactor knows, the more useful the Lore of the Forge can be. Even that can be skirted if the Malefactor has the help of an assistant who knows the desired Lore when they enchant an item.<br /> <br /> TL,DR: I view Lore-sharing as something that would happen in the here and now, because I like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-13T20:37:43-07:00","id":1481042,"title":"","content":"Not a bad idea, and I would definitely limit the type of Lores that can be remembered, and never allow them past 1 or 2. I can also see the Fiends clutching the Lore of Patterns like the Tremere do Thaumaturgy. Of course, they will probably give it up as a reward to anyone who breaks them out of Hell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}